==English==
{{was wotd|2019|September|29}}

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|en|nebʰ}}
From {{der|en|la|Neptūnius||of or pertaining to the Roman god Neptune}}, from {{m|la|Neptūnus||the Roman god Neptune}} (possibly ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*nebʰ-||to become damp, cloudy}}) + {{m|la|-ius|pos=''suffix forming {{glossary|adjective}}s from {{glossary|noun}}s''}}. The English word is cognate with {{cog|fr|neptunien||pertaining to the Roman god Neptune, pertaining to the sea, pertaining to Neptunism, Neptunian; proponent of Neptunism, Neptunist}}, {{cog|de|Neptunier||proponent of Neptunism, Neptunist}};<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n.'' and ''adj|id=126156|date=September 2003|nodot=yes}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=adj}}</ref> and is analysable as {{suffix|en|Neptune|ian}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/nɛpˈtjuː.nɪ.ən/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/nɛpˈt(j)u.ni.ən/|/-ˈtʃuː-/}}
* {{hyphenation|en|Nep|tun|i|an}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|Roman mythology}} Of or pertaining to [[Neptune]], the [[Roman#Adjective|Roman]] [[god]] of [[fresh water]] and the [[sea]], the [[counterpart]] of the [[Greek#Adjective|Greek]] god [[Poseidon]].
# {{lb|en|by extension|rare}} Of or pertaining to [[water#Noun|water]] or the sea.
# {{lb|en|by extension|geology}} [[form#Verb|Formed]] by the [[action]] of water.
#: {{ux|en|'''neptunian''' dyke}}
# {{lb|en|by extension|geology|historical}} Of, pertaining to, or [[support#Verb|supporting]] {{l|en|Neptunism||a [[discredited#Adjective|discredited]] [[theory]] that [[rock#Noun|rocks]] were formed from the [[crystallisation]] of [[mineral]]s in the early [[Earth]]'s [[ocean]]s}}.
# {{lb|en|astronomy}} Of or pertaining to the [[planet]] Neptune.

